to the stomach, as it's doing here. It's time to slow down a bit and digest.

467
00:43:54,460 --> 00:44:01,840
Normally this stretchy, J-shaped bag isn't much bigger than a fist. But after a big meal,

468
00:44:01,840 --> 00:44:08,930
it can expand to more than 20 times that size. For the next several hours, highly acidic

469
00:44:08,930 --> 00:44:14,850
gastric juices spew from the stomach's walls, breaking down proteins in our food, while muscle

470
00:44:14,850 --> 00:44:17,170
contractions knead and churn it into a pulp.

471
00:44:21,260 --> 00:44:25,440
The acid here is so strong the stomach must continuously secrete a layer of protective

472
00:44:25,440 --> 00:44:32,340
mucus so that it doesn't digest itself.

473
00:44:32,340 --> 00:44:39,310
It absorbs very few nutrients though.

474
00:44:39,310 --> 00:44:45,270
We pass into the 20-foot disassembly line of the small intestine, with the help of a specialized

475
00:44:45,270 --> 00:44:48,840
camera pill.

476
00:44:48,840 --> 00:44:54,700
For about five hours, foods building blocks are pushed, prodded, sprayed with digestive juices

477
00:44:54,700 --> 00:45:00,420
and rung like a rag here until its vital elements are forced through the intestinal wall and into

478
00:45:00,420 --> 00:45:10,050
the bloodstream. Most of our meals nutrients will flow directly to the liver, the

479
00:45:10,050 --> 00:45:17,750
body's largest internal organ. The liver breaks down, repackages and delivers nutrients to our

480
00:45:17,750 --> 00:45:25,920
cells for growth and power. Our bodies ultimately try to balance energy intake.

481
00:45:25,920 --> 00:45:36,480
But sometimes more goes in than out. The result? Fat. This is how fat looks on the

482
00:45:36,480 --> 00:45:45,920
inside and on the outside. It doesn't take a lot of excess

483
00:45:45,940 --> 00:45:51,880
calories to make you gain weight. Just 15 more a day than you need, about the amount

484
00:45:51,880 --> 00:46:01,210
in four pistachio nuts, will add a pound and a half of fat over a year. Once the small intestine

485
00:46:01,210 --> 00:46:06,050
has taken in everything worth ingesting, the rest is pushed along to the large intestine.

486
00:46:08,170 --> 00:46:16,400
Another 20 hours or so, the last of the water is absorbed, and billions of bacteria work

487
00:46:16,400 --> 00:46:18,240
to break down the remaining contents.

488
00:46:18,240 --> 00:46:27,880
Anything we can't digest gets flushed out of our bodies.

489
00:46:34,080 --> 00:46:36,560
The food's complicated journey has a larger purpose.

490
00:46:38,140 --> 00:46:43,160
Once we've extracted what we need to feed the incredible machine and got our cellular engines humming,

491
00:46:44,020 --> 00:46:46,540
it's nothing short of astounding what we can do with them,

492
00:46:47,160 --> 00:46:49,660
thanks to amazing contraptions called muscle.

493
00:46:49,660 --> 00:47:16,300
Next, the other booker.

